  "notes": "のろける is a casual verb used to describe talking proudly or lovingly about one's romantic partner. It often carries a slightly teasing nuance, implying the speaker is perhaps overdoing it.\n\nREGISTER:\nThis is an informal/colloquial word commonly used in casual conversation.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ～のことでのろける: to gush about someone\n- のろけ{話|ばなし}: stories bragging about one's relationship\n\nRELATED NOUN:\nのろけ refers to the act of bragging about one's relationship or such bragging itself.",
